# This repo is worked on from both Windows and macOS against one shared volume,
# so without a normalization rule each side rewrites whole files to its own line
# endings. That produced a `git status` listing 33 modified files whose content
# diff was empty — pure CRLF/LF churn that buries real changes and turns any
# `git commit -a` into a multi-thousand-line no-op.
#
# LF in the repository and in the working tree on every platform. Nothing here
# needs CRLF: there are no .bat/.cmd/.ps1 scripts, and the Docker build scripts
# must stay LF to run in their Linux images.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets, marked explicitly rather than left to git's auto-detection.
# opencode.db is a SQLite fixture the adapter tests read — normalizing it would
# corrupt the file rather than merely reformat it.
*.png   binary
*.ico   binary
*.icns  binary
*.db    binary
